P2PDMA advertise feature-flag gating -- compile the P2P advertise out on
pre-6.11 kernels.

The P2P advertise machinery lives in drivers/md (feature branch p2pdma-fixes)
and is present in BOTH featured variants the kit builds: the member-AND
advertise via raid1_can_advertise_p2pdma(), the md_bio_is_p2pdma() detector,
and the add-path re-gate helper raid1_p2pdma_clear_on_add(). On kernels without
BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA (pre-6.11, e.g. RHEL9/5.14, which also lack the
FOLL_PCI_P2PDMA O_DIRECT path) the whole advertise must compile out. Gate every
site on HAVE_BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA (dkms/Makefile.in feature_flags probe): the
helpers and both advertise sites (raid1_set_limits, raid10_set_queue_limits)
#ifdef out entirely; md_bio_is_p2pdma() folds to a constant false so its callers
(REQ_NOMERGE preserve, write-behind skip) still build;
raid1_p2pdma_clear_on_add() folds to an empty inline stub so the four call sites
become no-ops with no per-call gating.

The stage-1 fail-the-write COMPLETION arms (feature branch p2pdma: the
R1BIO_P2PError / R10BIO_P2PError end_write_request arms, the call_bio_endio /
raid_end_bio_io master-status overrides, the end_read_request read-fidelity
blocks) are gated separately in 0011-p2pdma-failwrite-arm-gating.patch, because
that arm code exists ONLY in the full stage-1 tree. This advertise-gating patch
applies to every p2pdma-bearing tree; 0011 self-selects to the stage-1 tree via
its raid10.c:R10BIO_P2PError .when guard. This patch's own .when guard keys on
raid1_can_advertise_p2pdma (present in both featured variants); on bare upstream
`master` the helper is absent and 0009 handles upstream's raw P2PDMA assignment
instead.

Source-level, not a header shim: it adds preprocessor structure to drivers/md.

diff --git a/md.h b/md.h
index bee2420..4daf5a1 100644
--- a/md.h
+++ b/md.h
@@ -39,8 +39,12 @@
  */
 static inline bool md_bio_is_p2pdma(struct bio *bio)
 {
+#ifdef HAVE_BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA
 	return bio_has_data(bio) && bio->bi_io_vec &&
 	       is_pci_p2pdma_page(bio->bi_io_vec->bv_page);
+#else
+	return false;
+#endif
 }
 /*
  * Number of guaranteed raid bios in case of extreme VM load:
diff --git a/raid1-10.c b/raid1-10.c
index 9113e8d..f6e2fb4 100644
--- a/raid1-10.c
+++ b/raid1-10.c
@@ -304,6 +304,7 @@ static inline bool raid1_should_handle_error(struct bio *bio)
 		bio->bi_status != BLK_STS_INVAL;
 }
 
+#ifdef HAVE_BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA
 /*
  * Advertise PCI P2PDMA only when every non-faulty member can do it.
  * BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA is excluded from BLK_FEAT_INHERIT_MASK, so md sets it
@@ -353,3 +354,7 @@ static void raid1_p2pdma_clear_on_add(struct mddev *mddev, struct md_rdev *rdev)
 	lim.features &= ~BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA;
 	queue_limits_commit_update(mddev->gendisk->queue, &lim);
 }
+#else
+static inline void raid1_p2pdma_clear_on_add(struct mddev *mddev,
+					     struct md_rdev *rdev) { }
+#endif
diff --git a/raid1.c b/raid1.c
index 0db5753..a3b3baf 100644
--- a/raid1.c
+++ b/raid1.c
@@ -3267,8 +3274,10 @@ static int raid1_set_limits(struct mddev *mddev)
 	err = mddev_stack_rdev_limits(mddev, &lim, MDDEV_STACK_INTEGRITY);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
+#ifdef HAVE_BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA
 	if (raid1_can_advertise_p2pdma(mddev))
 		lim.features |= BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA;
+#endif
 	return queue_limits_set(mddev->gendisk->queue, &lim);
 }
 
diff --git a/raid10.c b/raid10.c
index c142ee9..6c9e180 100644
--- a/raid10.c
+++ b/raid10.c
@@ -3999,8 +4006,10 @@ static int raid10_set_queue_limits(struct mddev *mddev)
 	err = mddev_stack_rdev_limits(mddev, &lim, MDDEV_STACK_INTEGRITY);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
+#ifdef HAVE_BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA
 	if (raid1_can_advertise_p2pdma(mddev))
 		lim.features |= BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA;
+#endif
 	return queue_limits_set(mddev->gendisk->queue, &lim);
 }
 
